# OHOS tests read upstream sources straight from the working tree and pin them by
# content hash (SHA256, and git blob SHA1 for vendored copies); the harness also strips
# ES module imports with a `\n`-terminated regex. Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true
# system-wide, which smudges these LF blobs to CRLF and turns every pinned byte check
# into a failure. Pin LF wherever a test compares bytes. Docs/ and the desktop C# build
# are not content-pinned, so they keep their .editorconfig crlf preference.
/ohos/** text eol=lf
/Source/** text eol=lf
/tools/** text eol=lf

# Two upstream files were committed with CRLF inside the blob itself, so they must be
# reproduced byte for byte rather than normalized.
/Source/MultiFunPlayer/UI/Controls/KeyframesHeatmap.xaml.cs -text
/Source/MultiFunPlayer/UI/Controls/KeyframesHeatmapToolTip.xaml.cs -text
